nri_cpu_balloons: hybrid-aware CPU reservation and balloon placement

Against intel/enterprise-agent-toolkit @0ecf67a. Prepared for upstream; not sent.
Apply from the EAT checkout root: git apply enterprise-agent-toolkit.patch

compute_reserved_cpus.sh assumes Xeon numbering, where the second half of each
NUMA node's CPU ids are the hyperthread siblings of the first half. Intel hybrid
client CPUs number siblings adjacently (0-1, 2-3, ...) and add E-cores without
siblings. On an i9-13900T (P-cores 0-15, E-cores 16-31) the 8-CPU default
reserves 0,1,2,3,16,17,18,19: two whole P-cores lost to system pods.

- compute_reserved_cpus.sh reads /sys/devices/system/node/node*/cpulist and each
  CPU's topology/thread_siblings_list, and reserves whole physical cores, lowest
  ids first. When /sys/devices/cpu_core and cpu_atom both list CPUs (hybrid) it
  takes E-cores first. Xeon layouts give the same lists as before (1 and 2 NUMA
  nodes, with and without HT, 3/7/8 CPUs). The i9-13900T now gets 16-23. It no
  longer needs lscpu.
- get_optimized_cpu_topology.yaml sets nri_hybrid_cpu from the same PMU files
  (grep, since sysfs files report a size even when empty). Set it yourself when
  you pass nri_reserved_cpu_list.
- generic-balloon-values.yaml.j2, only when nri_hybrid_cpu is true: vllm-balloon
  gets preferCoreType: performance, and a new agent-control-plane balloon type
  (preferCoreType: efficient, one balloon, at least 2 CPUs) takes the namespaces
  in nri_agent_namespaces, listed before "reserved" so they match first. The
  rendered values are unchanged on non-hybrid hosts.
- defaults/main.yaml: nri_agent_namespaces = genai-gateway (LiteLLM, Langfuse),
  redis, pgvector, agent-sandbox-system, openshell-system, openshell-sandboxes,
  flowise, as deployed by this repo.

Checks run: the script against fake sysfs trees (k3d-gpu tests/reserved_cpus_test.sh);
the template rendered for hybrid and Xeon, then helm template with chart
nri-resource-policy-balloons v0.14.0, and the BalloonsPolicy validated against
that chart's CRD schema; shellcheck v0.11.0. Not run on a live cluster.

